# Mobile first

United Strength is **mobile first**. Most members will book and browse on their phone. The mobile experience must be the best version of every screen; desktop is an enhancement, not the primary target.

## Design and build order

1. **Layout mobile first** — Default styles target small viewports (~320px–428px). Add `md:` / `lg:` (or min-width media queries) only to enhance larger screens.
2. **Touch first** — Tap targets at least 44×44px. Adequate spacing between links and buttons. No hover-only interactions.
3. **Navigation** — Hamburger or compact nav on mobile; full nav on desktop. Keep Reserve / Buy reachable without deep menus (sticky bar or prominent footer CTAs if needed).
4. **Typography** — Readable body size on mobile (16px minimum for inputs to avoid iOS zoom). Headlines scale up on desktop, not down on mobile.
5. **Media** — Heroes and images crop well on portrait; avoid critical copy in corners that safe-area or notches clip. Prefer `object-cover` with mobile-safe focal points.
6. **Forms** — Single column, full-width inputs, large submit buttons. Membership and contact forms must be usable one-handed.
7. **Embeds** — `/buy`, `/schedule`, `/account` must be full-width and scrollable on small screens; test iframe height on iOS Safari.

## Tailwind / CSS convention

```css
/* Prefer: base = mobile, then enhance */
.element { /* mobile styles */ }
@screen md { .element { /* desktop enhancements */ } }
```

Avoid `max-width` “desktop first” breakpoints unless fixing a specific desktop-only bug.

## Review checklist

Before marking UI done, verify on a **narrow viewport** (375px) and real mobile Safari/Chrome:

- No horizontal scroll (except intentional carousels)
- CTAs visible without excessive scrolling
- Nav and footer usable
- Embed pages bookable on phone

